What is the primary purpose of a ProtectedRoute component in React?

```jsx
import { Navigate } from 'react-router';
import Cookies from 'js-cookie';

const ProtectedRoute = ({ children }) => {
  const token = Cookies.get('jwt_token');
  if (token === undefined) {
    return <Navigate to="/login" replace />;
  }
  return children;
};

export default ProtectedRoute;
```

What happens after the given code executed, when an unauthenticated user tries to access a protected route?

